WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 4.4 · People, Culture & Volunteers
Onboarding

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Your first people shape what joining means for everyone who follows, so plan their start well.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:26.281
Onboarding helps a new person understand the mission, their role, the safeguards and the practical ways of working. Giving someone access to a folder is only a small part of it.

4
00:00:26.681 --> 00:00:27.281
Three stages of a good start

5
00:00:27.281 --> 00:00:39.352
First day: A welcome, equipment and accounts, and meeting a buddy who will guide them. For example: In the shared kitchen, a founder shows each new trainee the equipment and safety rules.

6
00:00:39.352 --> 00:00:49.570
First week: Essential training, core policies signed and an early, useful task. For example: The new trainee shadows two shifts, then shapes a batch of rolls alone.

7
00:00:49.570 --> 00:00:59.878
First month: Check understanding, review progress and ask what was missing. For example: After four weeks, a new trainee suggests a clearer hygiene checklist.

8
00:01:00.278 --> 00:01:00.878
Why it matters

9
00:01:00.878 --> 00:01:06.552
1. Your first people shape what joining means for everyone after them.

10
00:01:06.552 --> 00:01:10.744
2. Checking understanding protects participants, not just paperwork.

11
00:01:10.744 --> 00:01:17.419
3. Culture is set by everyday behaviour from the very first day.

12
00:01:17.819 --> 00:01:18.419
How you will use it

13
00:01:18.419 --> 00:01:23.722
1. One standard template, with steps added for each new role.

14
00:01:23.722 --> 00:01:28.656
2. Your safeguarding and data protection essentials, explained in person.

15
00:01:28.656 --> 00:01:34.589
3. Your check-ins: the first-month review becomes the first one.

16
00:01:34.989 --> 00:01:35.589
What to avoid

17
00:01:35.589 --> 00:01:39.781
Sending documents and assuming they were read.

18
00:01:39.781 --> 00:01:44.344
Waiting until someone joins to build the template.

19
00:01:44.344 --> 00:01:50.278
No buddy, so the newcomer has nobody to ask.

20
00:01:50.878 --> 00:01:52.678
You create a 30-day onboarding plan for your first person.

21
00:01:52.678 --> 00:01:56.678
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

22
00:01:58.178 --> 00:02:01.278
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
